Elwynn Survival: what the add-on held lets go when it can't, a slower lock-on turn, and a walk
toggle that isn't lost.

- Leaving the world (a logout) or a new UI VM (a ReloadUI, the add-on turned off) resets the action
  mouse, aim camera, lock-on and markers, and drops a scripted MouselookStart nothing is left to
  stop: the next screen has its cursor, and the hero doesn't keep steering or running.
- The body turns to a locked-on unit at 5 rad/s (was 9): quick enough to keep a foe in front,
  slow enough that one rolling past gets behind for a moment.
- A TOGGLERUN press refused while rooted or riding a spline (the action server roots a hero for a
  moment through many of its moves) waits and goes once it's off, instead of seeming to do nothing
  and leaving the walk stuck.

